    {
      "id": "claim_491df52c48ff465bb9c8e1be85a31fc3",
      "statement": "Rolling updates via deployer-side orchestrator stops are supported (SIGTERM per node, wait for healthy replacement), but three documented upgrade exceptions exist: v0.1.0→v0.2.0 (not rolling — endpoint and block-object changes make a mixed fleet unsafe), v0.3.0→v0.4.0 (not rolling — inner tunnel protracted onto plain HTTP and epoch-qualified KV rows are unreadable by older readers), and v0.2.1→v0.3.0 (rolling OK, but v0.3.0 cannot replicate to v0.2.x — a no-return commit unless the shutdown log shows `node-log close: sealed epoch`).",
